src/DPD-REACT/fix_rx.cpp:551-558 (FixRX::setup_pre_force) runs the ConcOld copy over ALL local atoms with no group test:
    for (int id = 0; id < nlocal; id++)
      for (int ispecies=0; ispecies<nspecies; ispecies++) {
        const auto atom_ind = species_ind_to_atom_prop_ind[ispecies];
        const auto atom_ind_old = species_ind_to_atom_prop_ind_old[ispecies];
        tmp = atom->dvector[atom_ind][id];
        atom->dvector[atom_ind_old][id] = tmp;
      }
and only afterwards restricts the zero-rate ODE to `if (mask[i] & groupbit)` (fix_rx.cpp:560-571).  The KOKKOS port has no such unconditional loop: src/KOKKOS/fix_rx_kokkos.cpp:1262-1264 wraps everything, including the ConcOld update at lines 1291-1299 (`d_dvector(atom_ind_old, i) = static_cast<KK_FLOAT>(tmp);`), in `if (d_mask(i) & groupbit)`, and src/KOKKOS/fix_rx_kokkos.cpp:1227-1233 (setup_pre_force) calls only solve_reactions().

src/KOKKOS/fix_rigid_small_kokkos.cpp:1628 `const bool host_holds_bookkeeping = (!setupflag || setup_host_rebuild);` -- false during a run -- and :1679-1708:
    memoryKK->grow_kokkos(k_bodyown, bodyown, nmax, "rigid/small:bodyown");
    ...
    k_bodyown.sync_host();
    k_atom2body.sync_host();
    k_bodytag.sync_host();
    k_xcmimage.sync_host();
    k_displace.sync_host();
with the comment at :1691-1697 justifying it as "right during a run, when the device copy is the current one".  That premise only holds on the DEVICE exchange path.  On the host path the class deliberately runs the base-class host code: pre_exchange() (fix_rigid_small_kokkos.cpp:239-253) sync_host()s every view, which CLEARS both DualView modify flags; CommBrick::exchange() then calls FixRigidSmall::copy_arrays()/unpack_exchange() (src/RIGID/fix_rigid_small.cpp:2828-2867, :3042-3095) which write bodytag/bodyown/xcmimage/displace through the raw host pointers WITHOUT touching the flags; only pre_neighbor() (fix_rigid_small_kokkos.cpp:662-673) later does modify_host()+sync<DeviceType>().  If Atom::grow() fires anywhere in that window (a proc receiving more atoms than nmax during exchange, or comm->borders() adding ghosts), grow_kokkos -> DualView::resize takes the device branch, because both flags are 0: lib/kokkos/containers/src/Kokkos_DualView.hpp:1027 `if (modified_flags(1) >= modified_flags(0)) resize_on_device(arg_prop);` and :1044 `h_view = create_mirror_view(typename t_host::memory_space(), d_view);` -- a brand-new, empty host allocation, device marked modified -- and the sync_host() calls above then overwrite the host arrays with the PRE-exchange device snapshot.  Compare AtomVecKokkos::grow(), which avoids exactly this by doing atomKK->sync(Device,ALL_MASK)/modified(Device,ALL_MASK) before its own resizes.  (No effect when host space == device space, i.e. Serial/OpenMP builds, where impl_dualview_is_single_device makes the mirror alias the device view.)

